 "parts": [
  "Nothing travels faster than light.",
  "And soon, light will need a full day to reach Voyager one.",
  "That distance is called one light-day.",
  "It's about sixteen billion miles.",
  "To feel that, start small.",
  "Light reaches the Moon in about one point three seconds.",
  "Mars: three to twenty-two minutes.",
  "Voyager one: twenty-four hours.",
  "It launched in September, nineteen seventy-seven.",
  "Years later, it turned around and photographed Earth from three point seven billion miles.",
  "Now it's more than four times farther.",
  "Its power drops about four watts every year.",
  "In September, engineers swapped three devices for lower-power ones.",
  "In October, ground antennas couldn't detect its signal on two scheduled tries.",
  "Then it came back.",
  "When it crosses one light-day, the spacecraft won't detect any change.",
  "NASA says the milestone is about distance, not time.",
  "It's a line we drew, not one it feels.",
  "Send it a question, and the answer comes back in about two days.",
  "What would you ask it?"
 ],
